+# Drift → Retrain → Canary Runbook (PoC)
+
+Purpose:
+- Automate detection of data drift, retrain a candidate model with HPO, validate via Great Expectations, deploy as a canary and automatically rollback if business metric degrades.
+
+Components (added by this patch):
+- services/drift/detector.py - drift detector using evidently, triggers Tekton PipelineRun
+- Tekton tasks & pipeline under ops/tekton/* for materialize → hpo-train → validate → package → deploy-canary
+- services/monitoring/canary_controller.py - monitors canary vs baseline via Prometheus and rolls back on degradation
+- Prometheus alert rule ops/prometheus/alerts_canary.yaml
+- scripts/trigger_pipeline_from_detector.sh helper
+
+Quickstart (staging):
+1. Ensure baseline dataset and latest sample URIs are set as environment variables for the detector:
+   - BASELINE_S3_URI, LATEST_S3_URI, EVIDENCE_BUCKET, DRIFT_THRESHOLD
+2. Deploy the drift detector as a Deployment:
+   - image: python:3.10 with dependencies (evidently, prometheus_client, boto3, requests)
+3. Install Tekton tasks and pipeline in cicd namespace:
+   - kubectl apply -f ops/tekton/tasks/*.yaml
+   - kubectl apply -f ops/tekton/pipelines/drift_retrain_canary_pipeline.yaml
+4. Deploy canary controller as a Deployment with permissions to delete deployments and S3 write:
+   - configure PROM_URL, CANARY_DEPLOYMENT, METRIC expressions, REL_DROP_THRESHOLD, EVIDENCE_BUCKET
+5. Start the detector: it will compute drift periodically and trigger a PipelineRun when DRIFT_THRESHOLD exceeded.
+
+Notes & safety:
+- The flow is PoC: in production, use robust auth for Tekton triggers, use IAM roles & IRSA for S3 access, and ensure cosign keys are stored securely (KMS/Vault).
+- HPO/training is resource-intensive; run in controlled spot/cluster with quotas.
+- Canary controller uses simple Prometheus expressions; adapt to your business metrics and SLOs.
+
